{
  "id": "COMPOUND:2628 - PROTEIN:558",
  "verbalization": "Pregnenolone is implicated in the regulation of 11-cis retinol dehydrogenase through a series of mechanistic pathways. The evidence suggests that Pregnenolone acts as a target of multiple compounds that ultimately influence the activity of 11-cis retinol dehydrogenase. Specifically, Pregnenolone is linked to Liver X Receptor (LXR) alpha and beta, which are targets of 2-[(4S)-4-hydroxy-3,6-dioxodioxan-4-yl]acetic acid and 5-alpha-androstane-3-beta,17beta-diol. These compounds are themselves targets of 11-cis retinol dehydrogenase, indicating a chain of interactions that may modulate the enzyme's activity. The presence of multiple targets and the involvement of LXR suggest a potential role in lipid metabolism and signaling, which could be relevant to the biological effects of Pregnenolone. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between Pregnenolone and 11-cis retinol dehydrogenase, emphasizing the need for further investigation into the precise mechanisms by which these interactions occur.",
